Known bugs

The regression tests (tests/run.sh) compare the tools' output with
reference copies in tests/ref, which record what the tools do today,
bugs included.  Each bug below names the reference files that show its
wrong output: fixing the bug changes them, so check the new output and
update the references (tests/run.sh -u) in the same commit, and remove
the entry from this file.

Comparisons with a NaN: IEEE 754 makes every comparison with a NaN
false but !=, but bcc09's floating point compare helpers (Fcomp,
Fcompd and Fcompf, in libc/bcc/fpcmp.s) set the condition codes as if
the left operand were greater, so a > b and a >= b are true when either
is a NaN; <, <=, == and != are right.  tests/ref/nancmp.run shows it
(> and >= should be 0 on every line).

No others are known.  (The entry that was here, that taking the address of a
direct-page object gave "LEAX <_foo", described nothing cc1 does: a
__direct variable's value is reached as <_foo, its address with
LDX #_foo, or LEAX _foo,U with -Mo, as tests/ref/direct.s and
direct-u.s show.)
